ibutes**:\n   - **Rule 3**: All quiet people are round. Since Dave is quiet, he must be round.\n   - **Rule 6**: If someone is quiet and round, they are red. Since Dave is quiet and round, he must be red.\n   - **Rule 2**: If someone is red and round, they are smart. Since Dave is red and round, he must be smart.\n\n3. **Applying Rule 9**:\n   - **Rule 9**: All quiet, smart people are nice. Since Dave is quiet and smart (from the above inferences), he must be nice.\n\nTherefore, Dave must be nice, making the statement \"Dave is not nice\" false. The correct answer is **B) False**.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
