 to check if Erin is furry, we need to see if any of the rules lead to Erin being furry or not.Let\'s go through the rules.\n\nFirst, rule 8: If something is rough and cold, then it\'s furry.Erin is cold, but is she rough?From rule 16, all cold things are rough.So since Erin is cold, she must be rough.Therefore, Erin is rough and cold.Applying rule 8: rough ∧ cold → furry.So that would mean Erin is furry.Wait, but hold on.Let me check if there\'s any conflicting information.\n\nWait, but Erin\'s attributes are blue, cold, round.Let me see if any other rule contradicts this.Let\'s see:\n\nRule 15 says blue and round things are not quiet.Since Erin is blue and round, she\'s not quiet.That\'s okay, because she\'s cold and maybe that\'s separate.\n\nNow, according to rule 8, since Erin is rough (because she\'s cold, rule 16) and cold, then she must be furry.So that would mean Erin is furry.So that would make the answer True (Option A).But wait, let me check again.\n\nWait, but maybe there\'s another rule that says something else.Let me go through the rules again to make sure.\n\nLooking at rule 16: All cold things are rough.So Erin is cold → rough.So Erin is rough.Then, rule 8 says if something is rough and cold, then it\'s furry.So since Erin is both, she must be furry.That seems to directly lead to her being furry.But let me check if any other rule negates that.\n\nWait, is there any rule that says something like "if blue, then not furry" or something conflicting?\n\nLooking at the given data:\n\nRule 12 says if Fiona is furry, then Fiona is blue.But that\'s about Fiona, not Erin.\n\nRule 10: If Dave is blue then he\'s furry.But Dave is already given as furry, but his blue status isn\'t stated.Since the rule is only if he is blue, but since he\'s not stated to be blue, maybe that\'s irrelevant here.\n\nRule 11: Quiet and blue things are big.But Erin isn\'t quiet, so that\'s okay.\n\nRule 9: Quiet and big → not round.Again, Erin isn\'t quiet, so that doesn\'t affect her.\n\nRule 14: All big things are cold.Dave is big, so he must be cold.Wait, but the initial statements don\'t say Dave is cold.Wait, hold on a second.Let me check the initial statements again.\n\nOriginal context:\n\nDave is big.Dave is furry.Erin is blue.Erin is cold.Erin is round.Fiona is quiet.Gary is rough.Then the rest are the rules.\n\nSo Dave is big, so according to rule 14 (All big things are cold), Dave must be cold.But the initial statements didn\'t say Dave is cold.So that\'s an inference.So Dave is cold, but that\'s not stated in the given info, but it\'s a conclusion from rule 14.But that\'s okay.\n\nBut back to Erin.Since she is cold, rule 16 gives her rough.Then rule 8 requires her to be furry.So that would mean Erin is furry, so the answer would be True (A).But wait, let me check if there\'s any rule that says something else about being furry for Erin.\n\nLooking at the given attributes of Erin: blue, cold, round, rough (from cold via rule 16).The question is whether she is furry.The only rule that would require her to be furry is rule 8, which applies here.So unless there\'s a rule that says she can\'t be furry, but I don\'t see any.Let me check all rules again.\n\nRule 15: blue and round → not quiet.She\'s not quiet, so that\'s okay.\n\nRule 16: cold → rough.So that\'s covered.\n\nRule 8 gives her furry because rough and cold.So unless there\'s another condition that prevents her from being furry, but I don\'t see any.Let me check if any rules about being blue and furry.For example, rule 12 is about Fiona: if Fiona is furry, then Fiona is blue.But that doesn\'t mean blue things must be furry.It\'s a one-way implication.So Erin being blue doesn\'t necessarily mean she\'s furry unless another rule says so.But in this case, rule 8 does require her to be furry because of rough and cold.So that\'s the key.\n\nTherefore, according to the rules, Erin must be furry, so the statement "Erin is furry" is true.Therefore, the answer should be A) True.Wait, but