equires smartness (premise 9: "If something is quiet, it is smart"). Since Gary is quiet, he must be smart. The premises do not restrict smartness to specific entities, so no contradiction arises.\n\nAll steps follow logically without contradictions. Therefore, the statement "Gary is quiet" is **true**. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 59%|#####8    | 352/600 [3:24:39<9:44:26, 141.40s/it]
