messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nDave is quiet. Fiona is big. Fiona is furry. Gary is round. Gary is young. Harry is quiet. Harry is rough. If someone is furry then they are rough. Big people are rough. If someone is rough then they are young. If someone is young and round then they are quiet. Big, young people are cold. Cold people are round. If someone is young and not furry then they are not round.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Dave is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>:\nOkay, let\'s try to tackle this problem step by step.So, the question is whether the statement "Dave is not big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.The options are A, B, or C. Alright, first I need to parse all the information provided and see how each of the individuals (Dave, Fiona, Gary, Harry) relate to the different attributes.\n\nFirst, let me list out all the given facts:\n\n1.Dave is quiet.\n2.Fiona is big.\n3.Fiona is furry.\n4.Gary is round.\n5.Gary is young.\n6.Harry is quiet.\n7.Harry is rough.\n8.If someone is furry, then they are rough.(Furry → Rough)\n9.Big people are rough.(Big → Rough)\n10.If someone is rough, then they are young.(Rough → Young)\n11.If someone is young and round, then they are quiet.(Young ∧ Round → Quiet)\n12.Big, young people are cold.(Big ∧ Young → Cold)\n13.Cold people are round.(Cold → Round)\n14.If someone is young and not furry, then they are not round.(Young ∧ ¬Furry → ¬Round)\n\nThe question is about Dave being not big.So we need to see if we can determine Dave\'s size (big or not) based on these rules.\n\nFirst, let\'s note down the attributes each person has:\n\n- Dave: Quiet\n- Fiona: Big, Furry\n- Gary: Round, Young\n- Harry: Quiet, Rough\n\nNow, let\'s see if there\'s any information that can link Dave to being big 