dence the bald eagle visits/visits the cow, this doesn\u2019t apply.\n   - **Conditional 13:** If the bald eagle visited itself, it would be \"nice\" (and thus \"big\" via statement 12). However, there\u2019s no contradiction here, as the bald eagle\u2019s traits (niceness/bigness) are unspecified.\n   - **Other conditionals (e.g., 14\u201317):** Focus on the cat, rabbit, and cow. None directly involve the bald eagle\u2019s self-visit.\n\n3. **Self-Visitation Consideration:**\n   - The problem allows entities to visit themselves (e.g., the rabbit is forced to visit itself via conditional 16). However, no rule explicitly allows or prohibits the bald eagle from doing so.\n   - No contradiction arises if the bald eagle visits itself (e.g., being \"nice\" doesn\u2019t conflict with given facts), and no rule prevents it either.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - Since the context provides **no information** confirming or denying the bald eagle\u2019s self-visit, its truth value is indeterminate. Thus, the answer is **C) Unknown**.",
