levant.\n\n6.If Gary is blue and Gary is round then Gary is not cold.\n   - Wait, Gary is green, which from rule 2 means he is round.But Gary\'s color is green, but is he blue?The context says Gary is green, not blue.Wait, let me check again.The given info says Gary is green.So Gary is not blue.Therefore, the condition "Gary is blue and Gary is round" would not apply here because Gary isn\'t blue.So that rule might not affect Gary in this case.\n\n7.All round people are not furry.\n   - So if someone is round, they are not furry.Dave is round, so not furry.Gary, being green, is round, so he\'s not furry either.\n\n8.If someone is cold and not furry then they are white.\n   - Let\'s see.Charlie is blue, so he is cold (from rule 4).Also, Charlie\'s fur?Well, the rules say all round people are not furry.But Charlie\'s roundness isn\'t stated.Let me check Charlie\'s attributes.The problem states Charlie is quiet and blue, but doesn\'t say if he\'s round.\n\nWait, let me go back step by step.Let\'s start with Charlie.\n\nCharlie is blue and quiet.Since he\'s blue, he is cold (rule 4).Now, to check if he is white, we need to see if he meets the conditions for being white.The only rule that mentions white is the last one: If someone is cold and not furry, then they are white.\n\nSo, to be white, Charlie must be cold and not furry.But cold he is (because blue).Now, is he not furry?\n\nTo determine if he\'s furry or not, we need to see if he\'s round.Because rule 7 says all round people are not furry.So if Charlie is round, then he is not furry, which would make him white (since he\'s cold).If he isn\'t round, then maybe he is furry, so the rule doesn\'t apply.\n\nWait, but rule 7 says all round people are not furry, but it doesn\'t say anything about non-round people.So if Charlie isn\'t round, then maybe he could be furry or not, but the rules don\'t specify.Hmm.\n\nBut let\'s check if Charlie is round.Let\'s see the rules that might affect Charlie\'s roundness.\n\nRule 1 